Hi,

You can even use offset = 0 to get more genes with higher fold changes 
but,  many of them will have very low intensities, will not be 
biologically relevant and can be artifacts that introduce noise in the 
functional analysis.

Unfortunately, using an offset or another will not solve the problem of 
the sample size. I recommend you to use offset = 50 (the default) and to 
check graphically the effect of different filters based on Fold Changes 
with an MA plot.

By the way, you do not need p.values to use FIESTA.

Best,

OLI




